  "_about": "v79.9 (B4): per institution module, the special laws expected in the graph -- the same list as the module's «laws» in data/institution_modules.json (a test keeps them equal). scripts/corpus_gaps.py --env .env prints the missing ones for ingestion; the parere prints one fixed line in §1 and §9 when a case's module has one missing (lawyer_method.MISSING_LAWS_LINE). «defaults»: the laws admitted for every civil or criminal case (Block C's family allowlist), checked the same way. v79.10 (A4): the amministrativo module -- L. 241/1990 and the TU edilizia d.P.R. 380/2001 (the c.p.a. is a code: always admitted, not a module law). v79.10 (A4, archive names): the archive's document names carry no law numbers -- each law maps to «archive_names», the exact names of its primary documents (a list: an edition changes the name), matched by whitespace-normalised equality only, never by number, expression or substring (src/rag/corpus_laws.py); [] when the law is not in the archive (unmapped: always missing, never guessed). «number», «year» and «aliases» only read the user's own words (family_gate.user_named, the «istituto» door). «codes»: the codes a module names by sigla (the c.p.a.), mapped the same way. The mappings are the user's (BRIEF 79.10). v79.19.6: the 21 documents ingested on 27 Nov 2026 (lavoro, locazioni, sanitario, procedura civile, penale, famiglia, bancario) mapped to their exact names; L. 108/1990, L. 223/1991 and d.lgs. 165/2001 added to the licenziamento module (the last also to amministrativo), L. 76/2016 to famiglia; every one of the 21 has a table entry in data/special_laws.json too (its family and signal).",
